<p>Thanks for bringing it to my attention, Cubey. I have switched around a few of the personas to attempt to make it less stereotypical; after all, men in the 18-25 bracket are the most likely to suffer mental health problems leading to suicide.</p>
<p>I'll also add the backstory of -2 as a bonus, if you like. In my head she is from a time before humanity ever left Africa - so she doesn't speak any language which the Foundation could possibly know, and she's absolutely petrified. This is probably a time which is quite far removed from the time of the customer, but this customer specified quite a lot of specific parameters for her - hence the algorithm having to travel quite a long way before it found someone to fit. The one thing they forgot to mention is 'make her come from my time'!</p>

